{% extends "@core/base.p2" %}

{% comment %}
  Shared error page skeleton.

  The reference ID is the whole point of this page. Everything specific about a
  failure (the table, the path, the upstream message) is in a log line the viewer
  cannot read and should not be able to, so this page's job is to hand them the
  one string that connects what they saw to what the server recorded. It sits in
  the article's footer because that is the last thing on the page and the first
  thing to paste into a bug report.

  The error text appears only when the framework says it may. That decision is
  passed in rather than read from a flag here, so this template stays correct if
  the disclosure rule changes; what it must never do is render a value it was
  handed without being told to. When it does appear it goes in a <pre>, since the
  text is a Go error chain, and the line breaks in that chain are the reason a
  wrapped paragraph would not be readable.
{% endcomment %}

{% block title %}{{ status }} {{ statusText }} · {{ siteTitle|default:"Application" }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<article>
  <header>
    <h1>{{ status }} {{ statusText }}</h1>
  </header>

  {% block detail %}{% endblock %}

  {% if errorDetail %}
  <pre>{{ errorDetail }}</pre>
  {% endif %}

  {% if requestId %}
  <footer>
    <p><small>Reference: <code>{{ requestId }}</code></small></p>
  </footer>
  {% endif %}
</article>
{% endblock %}
